{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Variables are tested in index order, 0 nearest the root. The table never holds two vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that test the same variable with the same children, nor a vertex whose children are equal, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each function has one vertex: two "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/Function","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" values are equal exactly when they are the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)          \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)              \/\/ 5","diagram.vertexCount(of: f)                            \/\/ 5: x0, x1, x2 and both constants","let g = diagram.restrict(f, variable: 2, to: false)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1","g == diagram.and(x0, x1)                              \/\/ true"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Functions are built by the mutating methods, which add vertices to the table and leave every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"existing function as it was; a function belongs to the table it was built in and its copies."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The table keeps every vertex it has made."}]}